    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1881" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄητος</span></b>  (B), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		only in phrase <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος ἄητον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.395
				</span></i>
			 (=
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος ἄᾱτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					1.217
				</span></i>
			); also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄητοι;</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκόρεστοι, ἄπληστοι</span>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀήτους:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγάλας</span> (<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				3
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄητος</span></b> 
				(C)&lt;*&gt;<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
			ἀκατάπαυστος</span>, Hdn Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.220
			</span></i>; perh. <i>insatiate</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄω</span>);
			cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴητος</span>.</div>
